< Role Based Access Control >
---> Role : Creating the previliges or permissions say, pods:view | svc: create&delete | cm:create& view. specified to only a namspace
---> Cluster-Role: This is for cluster-wide namespaces and obejects
---> Role Building: attaching the role to the user (to a specific name space)
---> Cluster Role Binding: attaching the role to the user all over the cluster

| kubectl config view | can find the list of users | default root user is minikube |

# to crete a user, we neeed a client-crtificate and a client-key

| openssl genrsa -out pavan.key 2048 | generates a key for user pavan |

| openssl req -new -key pavan.key -out pavan.csr -subj "/CN=pavan/O=group1" | to generate a client sign request |

| openssl x509 -req -in pavan.csr -CA ~/.minikube/ca.crt -CAkey ~/.minikube/ca.key -CAcreateserial -out pavan.crt -days 500 | to generate a client certificate for user pavan |

# Now we have to crete a user
| kubectl config set-credentials pavan --client-certificate=pavan.crt --client-key=pavan.key | creates a user using the previously created certificate and key |

# Now we need to create a context for the user to add the user to the cluster. This is used to switch from one user to another user.
# context name for minikube is minikube | can find using kubectl config view

| kubectl config set-context devops-practice --cluster=minikube --user=pavan | to create the context |

| kubectl config use-context devops-practice | to switch the context |

# the role is created but there are no permissions yet bcoz we didnot attach any permissions.

# manifest file for role:
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  name: dev-role
  namespace: dev
rules:
  - apiGroups: ["*"]
    resources: ["pods"]
    verbs: ["get", "list", "watch", "create"]

#now binding.yml
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: RoleBinding
metadata:
  name: pavan-rb
  namespace: dev
subjects:
  - kind: User
    name: pavan
    apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io
roleRef:
  kind: Role
  name: dev-role
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io

| kubectl auth can-i get po | output will be no since the user pavan does not have permission for default ns|

| kubectl auth can-i get po -n dev | output will be yes | similarly we can check our permissions to all objects |

# For cluster-role, the manifest file is similare.
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRole
metadata:
  name: dev-cluster-role #namespace is irrelavant
rules:
  - apiGroups: ["*"]
    resources: ["pods", "services"]
    verbs: ["get", "list", "watch", "create"]

# cluster-role-binding manifest file
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRoleBinding
metadata:
  name: pavan-crb
subjects:
  - kind: User
    name: pavan
    apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io
roleRef:
  kind: ClusterRole
  name: dev-cluster-role
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io






















